{
  "schemaVersion": 2,
  "name": "Sport",
  "theme": "sportdash",
  "_about": "After BMW's Live Cockpit Sport view (photos of the X3's own cluster, measured on a warped overlay), generated by design/gen_sport.py (edit that and regenerate): blue speed (0..200 mph) and red rev (0..7000 rpm, the M40i's own scale) brackets, each a bright outer line, a filling band, a dark gap and an inner line. The middle is black; 'Leave room for the map' cuts it see-through for BMW's map, inset 'holeInset' px with 'holeRadius' corners. Everything that isn't text is one shader (sdash). The brackets and the gear keep clear of the black box BMW draws at x 1406..1597, y 342..419, and of the hood over the top corners. Widget reference: shared/hud.js header. Right of the rpm scale the car ahead as a gauge (gapGauge, an upright box x 1836..1852 y 432..588 filled from the bottom, 0..150 m): the metres ride beside the top of the fill, and under the rail its speed against ours ({{accRel}}, minus = closing); the fill and numbers turn red while it closes faster than 10 km/h; nothing shows with no car ahead. The map window keeps a triangle in each corner black (holeCut), where BMW's own Sport view draws bracket ends, a gauge icon and hatched dial ends (car photo, Nov 7 2026). The bottom strip is two bars from its middle out: the throttle to the left (its last tenth red in kickdown), the brake to the right (while the brake lights are on, how hard the car slows, on a log scale). Left of the speed scale, mirroring the car-ahead box, two upright boxes in the shader (vbars, x 24..40 and 96..112, y 432..588): boost (BST, 0..1.5 bar, yellow) and the 12 V battery (BAT, its charge %, green), each value riding beside the top of its fill (the battery's in V). The bottom row: the clock at the left with the range beside it, coolant and outside temperature at the right; its middle (x 630..1290, centred under the strip's middle at x 960, clear of BMW's seat-belt light) shows the song title BMW's player shows, in the car's own font so any script works, cut with … when too long. The map window also keeps a strip along its left edge black (holeMask, x 418..482 y 408..445: just above the fuel gauge, below BMW's speed so its hundreds digit shows), where BMW's speed-limit sign pokes out (car photo, Nov 8 2026). Behind the gear a soft dark patch (holeFade) keeps BMW's map lines from running through it (car photo, Nov 8 2026). The scale numbers fade in as the value comes near (nearFade 1: full white at the label, their own colour one label away), as iDrive 8 does. The fuel gauge's marks are the tank in litres or gallons (config.tankLitres full and half, 0), its unit under the top mark.",
